      "rootProvision": "act:section:8",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(6)",
      "markerToken": "6",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 7,
      "sourceText": "In the event of a personal data breach, the Data Fiduciary shall give the Board and\neach affected Data Principal, intimation of such breach in such form and manner as may be\nprescribed.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:8:subsection:7",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:8",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:8",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(7)",
      "markerToken": "7",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 8,
      "sourceText": "A Data Fiduciary shall, unless retention is necessary for compliance with any law\nfor the time being in force,—",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:8:subsection:7:clause:a",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:8:subsection:7",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:8",
      "provisionLevel": "clause",
      "marker": "(a)",
      "markerToken": "a",
      "depth": 2,
      "order": 9,
      "sourceText": "erase personal data, upon the Data Principal withdrawing her consent or as\nsoon as it is reasonable to assume that the specified purpose is no longer being\nserved, whichever is earlier; and",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:8:subsection:7:clause:b",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:8:subsection:7",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:8",
      "provisionLevel": "clause",
      "marker": "(b)",
      "markerToken": "b",
      "depth": 2,
      "order": 10,
      "sourceText": "cause its Data Processor to erase any personal data that was made available\nby the Data Fiduciary for processing to such Data Processor.\nIllustrations.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:8:subsection:7:clause:b:item:i",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:8:subsection:7:clause:b",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:8",
      "provisionLevel": "item",
      "marker": "(I)",
      "markerToken": "I",
      "depth": 4,
      "order": 11,
      "sourceText": "X, an individual, registers herself on an online marketplace operated by Y, an\ne-commerce service provider. X gives her consent to Y for the processing of her personal\ndata for selling her used car. The online marketplace helps conclude the sale. Y shall no\nlonger retain her personal data.",
      "crossReferences": [],
      "_has_children": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:8:subsection:7:clause:b:item:ii",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:8:subsection:7:clause:b",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:8",
      "provisionLevel": "item",
      "marker": "(II)",
      "markerToken": "II",
      "depth": 4,
      "order": 12,
      "sourceText": "X, an individual, decides to close her savings account with Y, a bank. Y is required\nby law applicable to banks to maintain the record of the identity of its clients for a period of\nten years beyond closing of accounts. Since retention is necessary for compliance with law,\nY shall retain X’s personal data for the said period.",
      "crossReferences": [],
      "_has_children": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:8:subsection:8",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:8",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:8",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(8)",
      "markerToken": "8",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 13,
      "sourceText": "The purpose referred to in clause (a) of sub-section (7) shall be deemed to no\nlonger be served, if the Data Principal does not––",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:8:subsection:8:clause:a",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:8:subsection:8",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:8",
      "provisionLevel": "clause",
      "marker": "(a)",
      "markerToken": "a",
      "depth": 2,
      "order": 14,
      "sourceText": "approach the Data Fiduciary for the performance of the specified purpose;\nand",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:8:subsection:8:clause:b",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:8:subsection:8",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:8",
      "provisionLevel": "clause",
      "marker": "(b)",
      "markerToken": "b",
      "depth": 2,
      "order": 15,
      "sourceText": "exercise any of her rights in relation to such processing,\nfor such time period as may be prescribed, and different time periods may be prescribed for\ndifferent classes of Data Fiduciaries and for different purposes.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:8:subsection:9",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:8",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:8",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(9)",
      "markerToken": "9",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 16,
      "sourceText": "A Data Fiduciary shall publish, in such manner as may be prescribed, the business\ncontact information of a Data Protection Officer, if applicable, or a person who is able to\nanswer on behalf of the Data Fiduciary, the questions, if any, raised by the Data Principal\nabout the processing of her personal data.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:8:subsection:10",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:8",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:8",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(10)",
      "markerToken": "10",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 17,
      "sourceText": "A Data Fiduciary shall establish an effective mechanism to redress the grievances\nof Data Principals.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:8:subsection:11",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:8",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:8",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(11)",
      "markerToken": "11",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 18,
      "sourceText": "For the purposes of this section, it is hereby clarified that a Data Principal shall be\nconsidered as not having approached the Data Fiduciary for the performance of the specified\npurpose, in any period during which she has not initiated contact with the Data Fiduciary\nfor such performance, in person or by way of communication in electronic or physical form.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:9",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:chapter:ii",
      "provisionLevel": "section",
      "sectionNumber": 9,
      "title": "Processing of personal data of children",
      "sourcePages": {
        "start": 8,
        "end": 8
      },
      "extractedSourceText": "9. (1) The Data Fiduciary shall, before processing any personal data of a child or a\nperson with disability who has a lawful guardian obtain verifiable consent of the parent of\nsuch child or the lawful guardian, as the case may be, in such manner as may be prescribed.\nExplanation.—For the purpose of this sub-section, the expression “consent of the\nparent” includes the consent of lawful guardian, wherever applicable.\n(2) A Data Fiduciary shall not undertake such processing of personal data that is\nlikely to cause any detrimental effect on the well-being of a child.\n(3) A Data Fiduciary shall not undertake tracking or behavioural monitoring of children\nor targeted advertising directed at children.\n(4) The provisions of sub-sections (1) and (3) shall not be applicable to processing of\npersonal data of a child by such classes of Data Fiduciaries or for such purposes, and\nsubject to such conditions, as may be prescribed.\n(5) The Central Government may, if satisfied that a Data Fiduciary has ensured that its\nprocessing of personal data of children is done in a manner that is verifiably safe, notify for\nsuch processing by such Data Fiduciary the age above which that Data Fiduciary shall be\nexempt from the applicability of all or any of the obligations under sub-sections (1) and (3)\nin respect of processing by that Data Fiduciary as the notification may specify.",
      "bodyText": "(1) The Data Fiduciary shall, before processing any personal data of a child or a\nperson with disability who has a lawful guardian obtain verifiable consent of the parent of\nsuch child or the lawful guardian, as the case may be, in such manner as may be prescribed.\nExplanation.—For the purpose of this sub-section, the expression “consent of the\nparent” includes the consent of lawful guardian, wherever applicable.\n(2) A Data Fiduciary shall not undertake such processing of personal data that is\nlikely to cause any detrimental effect on the well-being of a child.\n(3) A Data Fiduciary shall not undertake tracking or behavioural monitoring of children\nor targeted advertising directed at children.\n(4) The provisions of sub-sections (1) and (3) shall not be applicable to processing of\npersonal data of a child by such classes of Data Fiduciaries or for such purposes, and\nsubject to such conditions, as may be prescribed.\n(5) The Central Government may, if satisfied that a Data Fiduciary has ensured that its\nprocessing of personal data of children is done in a manner that is verifiably safe, notify for\nsuch processing by such Data Fiduciary the age above which that Data Fiduciary shall be\nexempt from the applicability of all or any of the obligations under sub-sections (1) and (3)\nin respect of processing by that Data Fiduciary as the notification may specify.",
      "leadInText": "",
      "textStatus": "PDF-extracted; Gazette PDF remains authoritative",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:9:subsection:1",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
