      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(1)",
      "markerToken": "1",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 0,
      "sourceText": "The salary, allowances and other terms and conditions of service of the\nChairperson and other Members shall be such as may be prescribed, and shall not be varied\nto their disadvantage after their appointment.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:20:subsection:2",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:20",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:20",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(2)",
      "markerToken": "2",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 1,
      "sourceText": "The Chairperson and other Members shall hold office for a term of two years and\nshall be eligible for re-appointment.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:21",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:chapter:v",
      "provisionLevel": "section",
      "sectionNumber": 21,
      "title": "Disqualifications for appointment and continuation as Chairperson and Members",
      "sourcePages": {
        "start": 13,
        "end": 13
      },
      "extractedSourceText": "21. (1) A person shall be disqualified for being appointed and continued as the\nChairperson or a Member, if she—\n(a) has been adjudged as an insolvent;\n(b) has been convicted of an offence, which in the opinion of the Central\nGovernment, involves moral turpitude;\n(c) has become physically or mentally incapable of acting as a Member;\n(d) has acquired such financial or other interest, as is likely to affect prejudicially\nher functions as a Member; or\n(e) has so abused her position as to render her continuance in office prejudicial\nto the public interest.\n(2) The Chairperson or Member shall not be removed from her office by the Central\nGovernment unless she has been given an opportunity of being heard in the matter.",
      "bodyText": "(1) A person shall be disqualified for being appointed and continued as the\nChairperson or a Member, if she—\n(a) has been adjudged as an insolvent;\n(b) has been convicted of an offence, which in the opinion of the Central\nGovernment, involves moral turpitude;\n(c) has become physically or mentally incapable of acting as a Member;\n(d) has acquired such financial or other interest, as is likely to affect prejudicially\nher functions as a Member; or\n(e) has so abused her position as to render her continuance in office prejudicial\nto the public interest.\n(2) The Chairperson or Member shall not be removed from her office by the Central\nGovernment unless she has been given an opportunity of being heard in the matter.",
      "leadInText": "",
      "textStatus": "PDF-extracted; Gazette PDF remains authoritative",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:21:subsection:1",
