      "markerToken": "2",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 6,
      "sourceText": "The Chairperson or Member shall not be removed from her office by the Central\nGovernment unless she has been given an opportunity of being heard in the matter.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:22",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:chapter:v",
      "provisionLevel": "section",
      "sectionNumber": 22,
      "title": "Resignation by Chairperson or Member and filling of vacancy",
      "sourcePages": {
        "start": 13,
        "end": 13
      },
      "extractedSourceText": "22. (1) The Chairperson or any other Member may give notice in writing to the Central\nGovernment of resigning from her office, and such resignation shall be effective from the\ndate on which the Central Government permits her to relinquish office, or upon expiry of a\nperiod of three months from the date of receipt of such notice, or upon a duly appointed\nsuccessor entering upon her office, or upon the expiry of the term of her office, whichever\nis earliest.\n(2) A vacancy caused by the resignation or removal or death of the Chairperson or\nany other Member, or otherwise, shall be filled by fresh appointment in accordance with the\nprovisions of this Act.\n(3) The Chairperson and any other Member shall not, for a period of one year from the\ndate on which they cease to hold such office, except with the previous approval of the\nCentral Government, accept any employment, and shall also disclose to the Central\nGovernment any subsequent acceptance of employment with any Data Fiduciary against\nwhom proceedings were initiated by or before such Chairperson or other Member.",
      "bodyText": "(1) The Chairperson or any other Member may give notice in writing to the Central\nGovernment of resigning from her office, and such resignation shall be effective from the\ndate on which the Central Government permits her to relinquish office, or upon expiry of a\nperiod of three months from the date of receipt of such notice, or upon a duly appointed\nsuccessor entering upon her office, or upon the expiry of the term of her office, whichever\nis earliest.\n(2) A vacancy caused by the resignation or removal or death of the Chairperson or\nany other Member, or otherwise, shall be filled by fresh appointment in accordance with the\nprovisions of this Act.\n(3) The Chairperson and any other Member shall not, for a period of one year from the\ndate on which they cease to hold such office, except with the previous approval of the\nCentral Government, accept any employment, and shall also disclose to the Central\nGovernment any subsequent acceptance of employment with any Data Fiduciary against\nwhom proceedings were initiated by or before such Chairperson or other Member.",
      "leadInText": "",
      "textStatus": "PDF-extracted; Gazette PDF remains authoritative",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:22:subsection:1",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:22",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:22",
