      "markerToken": "2",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 1,
      "sourceText": "A vacancy caused by the resignation or removal or death of the Chairperson or\nany other Member, or otherwise, shall be filled by fresh appointment in accordance with the\nprovisions of this Act.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:22:subsection:3",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:22",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:22",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(3)",
      "markerToken": "3",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 2,
      "sourceText": "The Chairperson and any other Member shall not, for a period of one year from the\ndate on which they cease to hold such office, except with the previous approval of the\nCentral Government, accept any employment, and shall also disclose to the Central\nGovernment any subsequent acceptance of employment with any Data Fiduciary against\nwhom proceedings were initiated by or before such Chairperson or other Member.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:23",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:chapter:v",
      "provisionLevel": "section",
      "sectionNumber": 23,
      "title": "Proceedings of Board",
      "sourcePages": {
        "start": 13,
        "end": 13
      },
      "extractedSourceText": "23. (1) The Board shall observe such procedure in regard to the holding of and\ntransaction of business at its meetings, including by digital means, and authenticate its\norders, directions and instruments in such manner as may be prescribed.\n(2) No act or proceeding of the Board shall be invalid merely by reason of—\n(a) any vacancy in or any defect in the constitution of the Board;\n(b) any defect in the appointment of a person acting as the Chairperson or other\nMember of the Board; or\n(c) any irregularity in the procedure of the Board, which does not affect the\nmerits of the case.\n(3) When the Chairperson is unable to discharge her functions owing to absence,\nillness or any other cause, the senior-most Member shall discharge the functions of the\nChairperson until the date on which the Chairperson resumes her duties.",
      "bodyText": "(1) The Board shall observe such procedure in regard to the holding of and\ntransaction of business at its meetings, including by digital means, and authenticate its\norders, directions and instruments in such manner as may be prescribed.\n(2) No act or proceeding of the Board shall be invalid merely by reason of—\n(a) any vacancy in or any defect in the constitution of the Board;\n(b) any defect in the appointment of a person acting as the Chairperson or other\nMember of the Board; or\n(c) any irregularity in the procedure of the Board, which does not affect the\nmerits of the case.\n(3) When the Chairperson is unable to discharge her functions owing to absence,\nillness or any other cause, the senior-most Member shall discharge the functions of the\nChairperson until the date on which the Chairperson resumes her duties.",
      "leadInText": "",
      "textStatus": "PDF-extracted; Gazette PDF remains authoritative",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:23:subsection:1",
