      "@id": "act:section:28:subsection:3",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:28",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:28",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(3)",
      "markerToken": "3",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 2,
      "sourceText": "The Board shall determine whether there are sufficient grounds to proceed with an\ninquiry.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:28:subsection:4",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:28",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:28",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(4)",
      "markerToken": "4",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 3,
      "sourceText": "In case the Board determines that there are insufficient grounds, it may, for reasons\nto be recorded in writing, close the proceedings.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:28:subsection:5",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:28",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:28",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(5)",
      "markerToken": "5",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 4,
      "sourceText": "In case the Board determines that there are sufficient grounds to proceed with\ninquiry, it may, for reasons to be recorded in writing, inquire into the affairs of any person for\nascertaining whether such person is complying with or has complied with the provisions of\nthis Act.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:28:subsection:6",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:28",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:28",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(6)",
      "markerToken": "6",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 5,
      "sourceText": "The Board shall conduct such inquiry following the principles of natural justice\nand shall record reasons for its actions during the course of such inquiry.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:28:subsection:7",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:28",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:28",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(7)",
      "markerToken": "7",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 6,
      "sourceText": "For the purposes of discharging its functions under this Act, the Board shall have\nthe same powers as are vested in a civil court under the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908, in\nrespect of matters relating to—",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:28:subsection:7:clause:a",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:28:subsection:7",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:28",
      "provisionLevel": "clause",
      "marker": "(a)",
      "markerToken": "a",
      "depth": 2,
      "order": 7,
      "sourceText": "summoning and enforcing the attendance of any person and examining her\non oath;",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:28:subsection:7:clause:b",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:28:subsection:7",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:28",
      "provisionLevel": "clause",
      "marker": "(b)",
      "markerToken": "b",
      "depth": 2,
      "order": 8,
      "sourceText": "receiving evidence of affidavit requiring the discovery and production of\ndocuments;",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:28:subsection:7:clause:c",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:28:subsection:7",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:28",
      "provisionLevel": "clause",
      "marker": "(c)",
      "markerToken": "c",
      "depth": 2,
      "order": 9,
      "sourceText": "inspecting any data, book, document, register, books of account or any\nother document; and",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:28:subsection:7:clause:d",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:28:subsection:7",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:28",
      "provisionLevel": "clause",
      "marker": "(d)",
      "markerToken": "d",
      "depth": 2,
      "order": 10,
      "sourceText": "such other matters as may be prescribed.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:28:subsection:8",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:28",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:28",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(8)",
      "markerToken": "8",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 11,
      "sourceText": "The Board or its officers shall not prevent access to any premises or take into\ncustody any equipment or any item that may adversely affect the day-to-day functioning of\na person.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:28:subsection:9",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:28",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:28",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(9)",
      "markerToken": "9",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 12,
      "sourceText": "The Board may require the services of any police officer or any officer of the\nCentral Government or a State Government to assist it for the purposes of this section and\nit shall be the duty of every such officer to comply with such requisition.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:28:subsection:10",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:28",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:28",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(10)",
      "markerToken": "10",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 13,
      "sourceText": "During the course of the inquiry, if the Board considers it necessary, it may for\nreasons to be recorded in writing, issue interim orders after giving the person concerned an\nopportunity of being heard.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:28:subsection:11",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:28",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:28",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(11)",
      "markerToken": "11",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 14,
      "sourceText": "On completion of the inquiry and after giving the person concerned an opportunity\nof being heard, the Board may for reasons to be recorded in writing, either close the\nproceedings or proceed in accordance with section 33.",
      "crossReferences": [
        {
          "referenceKind": "section",
          "sourcePhrase": "section 33",
          "targetDocument": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
          "target": "act:section:33",
          "resolutionStatus": "internal-resolved-root",
          "context": "On completion of the inquiry and after giving the person concerned an opportunity of being heard, the Board may for reasons to be recorded in writing, either close the proceedings or proceed in accordance with section 33."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:28:subsection:12",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:28",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:28",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(12)",
      "markerToken": "12",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 15,
      "sourceText": "At any stage after receipt of a complaint, if the Board is of the opinion that the\ncomplaint is false or frivolous, it may issue a warning or impose costs on the complainant.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:29",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:chapter:vii",
      "provisionLevel": "section",
      "sectionNumber": 29,
      "title": "Appeal to Appellate Tribunal",
      "sourcePages": {
        "start": 15,
        "end": 16
      },
      "extractedSourceText": "29. (1) Any person aggrieved by an order or direction made by the Board under this\nAct may prefer an appeal before the Appellate Tribunal.\n(2) Every appeal under sub-section (1) shall be filed within a period of sixty days from\nthe date of receipt of the order or direction appealed against and it shall be in such form and\nmanner and shall be accompanied by such fee as may be prescribed.\n(3) The Appellate Tribunal may entertain an appeal after the expiry of the period\nspecified in sub-section (2), if it is satisfied that there was sufficient cause for not preferring\nthe appeal within that period.\n(4) On receipt of an appeal under sub-section (1), the Appellate Tribunal may, after\ngiving the parties to the appeal, an opportunity of being heard, pass such orders thereon as\nit thinks fit, confirming, modifying or setting aside the order appealed against.\n(5) The Appellate Tribunal shall send a copy of every order made by it to the Board\nand to the parties to the appeal.\n(6) The appeal filed before the Appellate Tribunal under sub-section (1) shall be dealt\nwith by it as expeditiously as possible and endeavour shall be made by it to dispose of the\nappeal finally within six months from the date on which the appeal is presented to it.\n(7) Where any appeal under sub-section (6) could not be disposed of within the\nperiod of six months, the Appellate Tribunal shall record its reasons in writing for not\ndisposing of the appeal within that period.\n(8) Without prejudice to the provisions of section 14A and section 16 of the Telecom\nRegulatory Authority of India Act, 1997, the Appellate Tribunal shall deal with an appeal\nunder this section in accordance with such procedure as may be prescribed.\n(9) Where an appeal is filed against the orders of the Appellate Tribunal under this\nAct, the provisions of section 18 of the Telecom Regulatory Authority of India Act, 1997\nshall apply.\n(10) In respect of appeals filed under the provisions of this Act, the Appellate Tribunal\nshall, as far as practicable, function as a digital office, with the receipt of appeal, hearing and\npronouncement of decisions in respect of the same being digital by design.",
      "bodyText": "(1) Any person aggrieved by an order or direction made by the Board under this\nAct may prefer an appeal before the Appellate Tribunal.\n(2) Every appeal under sub-section (1) shall be filed within a period of sixty days from\nthe date of receipt of the order or direction appealed against and it shall be in such form and\nmanner and shall be accompanied by such fee as may be prescribed.\n(3) The Appellate Tribunal may entertain an appeal after the expiry of the period\nspecified in sub-section (2), if it is satisfied that there was sufficient cause for not preferring\nthe appeal within that period.\n(4) On receipt of an appeal under sub-section (1), the Appellate Tribunal may, after\ngiving the parties to the appeal, an opportunity of being heard, pass such orders thereon as\nit thinks fit, confirming, modifying or setting aside the order appealed against.\n(5) The Appellate Tribunal shall send a copy of every order made by it to the Board\nand to the parties to the appeal.\n(6) The appeal filed before the Appellate Tribunal under sub-section (1) shall be dealt\nwith by it as expeditiously as possible and endeavour shall be made by it to dispose of the\nappeal finally within six months from the date on which the appeal is presented to it.\n(7) Where any appeal under sub-section (6) could not be disposed of within the\nperiod of six months, the Appellate Tribunal shall record its reasons in writing for not\ndisposing of the appeal within that period.\n(8) Without prejudice to the provisions of section 14A and section 16 of the Telecom\nRegulatory Authority of India Act, 1997, the Appellate Tribunal shall deal with an appeal\nunder this section in accordance with such procedure as may be prescribed.\n(9) Where an appeal is filed against the orders of the Appellate Tribunal under this\nAct, the provisions of section 18 of the Telecom Regulatory Authority of India Act, 1997\nshall apply.\n(10) In respect of appeals filed under the provisions of this Act, the Appellate Tribunal\nshall, as far as practicable, function as a digital office, with the receipt of appeal, hearing and\npronouncement of decisions in respect of the same being digital by design.",
      "leadInText": "",
      "textStatus": "PDF-extracted; Gazette PDF remains authoritative",
      "crossReferences": [
        {
          "referenceKind": "section",
          "sourcePhrase": "section 14A",
          "targetDocument": "ext:trai-act-1997",
          "resolutionStatus": "external-resolved-document",
          "context": "(8) Without prejudice to the provisions of section 14A and section 16 of the Telecom Regulatory Authority of India Act, 1997, the Appellate Tribunal shall deal with an appeal under this section in accordance with such procedure as may be prescribed."
        },
        {
          "referenceKind": "section",
          "sourcePhrase": "section 16",
          "targetDocument": "ext:trai-act-1997",
          "resolutionStatus": "external-resolved-document",
          "context": "(8) Without prejudice to the provisions of section 14A and section 16 of the Telecom Regulatory Authority of India Act, 1997, the Appellate Tribunal shall deal with an appeal under this section in accordance with such procedure as may be prescribed."
        },
        {
          "referenceKind": "section",
          "sourcePhrase": "section 18",
          "targetDocument": "ext:trai-act-1997",
          "resolutionStatus": "external-resolved-document",
          "context": "(9) Where an appeal is filed against the orders of the Appellate Tribunal under this Act, the provisions of section 18 of the Telecom Regulatory Authority of India Act, 1997 shall apply."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:29:subsection:1",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:29",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:29",
