      "markerToken": "1",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 0,
      "sourceText": "Any person aggrieved by an order or direction made by the Board under this\nAct may prefer an appeal before the Appellate Tribunal.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:29:subsection:2",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:29",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:29",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(2)",
      "markerToken": "2",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 1,
      "sourceText": "Every appeal under sub-section (1) shall be filed within a period of sixty days from\nthe date of receipt of the order or direction appealed against and it shall be in such form and\nmanner and shall be accompanied by such fee as may be prescribed.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:29:subsection:3",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:29",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:29",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(3)",
      "markerToken": "3",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 2,
      "sourceText": "The Appellate Tribunal may entertain an appeal after the expiry of the period\nspecified in sub-section (2), if it is satisfied that there was sufficient cause for not preferring\nthe appeal within that period.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:29:subsection:4",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:29",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:29",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(4)",
      "markerToken": "4",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 3,
      "sourceText": "On receipt of an appeal under sub-section (1), the Appellate Tribunal may, after\ngiving the parties to the appeal, an opportunity of being heard, pass such orders thereon as\nit thinks fit, confirming, modifying or setting aside the order appealed against.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:29:subsection:5",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:29",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:29",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(5)",
      "markerToken": "5",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 4,
      "sourceText": "The Appellate Tribunal shall send a copy of every order made by it to the Board\nand to the parties to the appeal.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:29:subsection:6",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:29",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:29",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(6)",
      "markerToken": "6",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 5,
      "sourceText": "The appeal filed before the Appellate Tribunal under sub-section (1) shall be dealt\nwith by it as expeditiously as possible and endeavour shall be made by it to dispose of the\nappeal finally within six months from the date on which the appeal is presented to it.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:29:subsection:7",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:29",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:29",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(7)",
      "markerToken": "7",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 6,
      "sourceText": "Where any appeal under sub-section (6) could not be disposed of within the\nperiod of six months, the Appellate Tribunal shall record its reasons in writing for not\ndisposing of the appeal within that period.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:29:subsection:8",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:29",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:29",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(8)",
      "markerToken": "8",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 7,
      "sourceText": "Without prejudice to the provisions of section 14A and section 16 of the Telecom\nRegulatory Authority of India Act, 1997, the Appellate Tribunal shall deal with an appeal\nunder this section in accordance with such procedure as may be prescribed.",
      "crossReferences": [
        {
          "referenceKind": "section",
          "sourcePhrase": "section 14A",
          "targetDocument": "ext:trai-act-1997",
          "resolutionStatus": "external-resolved-document",
          "context": "Without prejudice to the provisions of section 14A and section 16 of the Telecom Regulatory Authority of India Act, 1997, the Appellate Tribunal shall deal with an appeal under this section in accordance with such procedure as may be prescribed."
        },
        {
          "referenceKind": "section",
          "sourcePhrase": "section 16",
          "targetDocument": "ext:trai-act-1997",
          "resolutionStatus": "external-resolved-document",
          "context": "Without prejudice to the provisions of section 14A and section 16 of the Telecom Regulatory Authority of India Act, 1997, the Appellate Tribunal shall deal with an appeal under this section in accordance with such procedure as may be prescribed."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:29:subsection:9",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:29",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:29",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(9)",
      "markerToken": "9",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 8,
      "sourceText": "Where an appeal is filed against the orders of the Appellate Tribunal under this\nAct, the provisions of section 18 of the Telecom Regulatory Authority of India Act, 1997\nshall apply.",
      "crossReferences": [
        {
          "referenceKind": "section",
          "sourcePhrase": "section 18",
          "targetDocument": "ext:trai-act-1997",
          "resolutionStatus": "external-resolved-document",
          "context": "Where an appeal is filed against the orders of the Appellate Tribunal under this Act, the provisions of section 18 of the Telecom Regulatory Authority of India Act, 1997 shall apply."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:29:subsection:10",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:29",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:29",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(10)",
      "markerToken": "10",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 9,
      "sourceText": "In respect of appeals filed under the provisions of this Act, the Appellate Tribunal\nshall, as far as practicable, function as a digital office, with the receipt of appeal, hearing and\npronouncement of decisions in respect of the same being digital by design.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:30",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:chapter:vii",
      "provisionLevel": "section",
      "sectionNumber": 30,
      "title": "Orders passed by Appellate Tribunal to be executable as decree",
      "sourcePages": {
        "start": 16,
        "end": 16
      },
      "extractedSourceText": "30. (1) An order passed by the Appellate Tribunal under this Act shall be executable\nby it as a decree of civil court, and for this purpose, the Appellate Tribunal shall have all the\npowers of a civil court.\n(2) Notwithstanding anything contained in sub-section (1), the Appellate Tribunal\nmay transmit any order made by it to a civil court having local jurisdiction and such civil\ncourt shall execute the order as if it were a decree made by that court.",
      "bodyText": "(1) An order passed by the Appellate Tribunal under this Act shall be executable\nby it as a decree of civil court, and for this purpose, the Appellate Tribunal shall have all the\npowers of a civil court.\n(2) Notwithstanding anything contained in sub-section (1), the Appellate Tribunal\nmay transmit any order made by it to a civil court having local jurisdiction and such civil\ncourt shall execute the order as if it were a decree made by that court.",
      "leadInText": "",
      "textStatus": "PDF-extracted; Gazette PDF remains authoritative",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:30:subsection:1",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:30",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:30",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(1)",
      "markerToken": "1",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 0,
      "sourceText": "An order passed by the Appellate Tribunal under this Act shall be executable\nby it as a decree of civil court, and for this purpose, the Appellate Tribunal shall have all the\npowers of a civil court.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:30:subsection:2",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:30",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:30",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(2)",
      "markerToken": "2",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 1,
      "sourceText": "Notwithstanding anything contained in sub-section (1), the Appellate Tribunal\nmay transmit any order made by it to a civil court having local jurisdiction and such civil\ncourt shall execute the order as if it were a decree made by that court.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:31",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:chapter:vii",
      "provisionLevel": "section",
      "sectionNumber": 31,
      "title": "Alternate dispute resolution",
      "sourcePages": {
        "start": 16,
        "end": 16
      },
      "extractedSourceText": "31. If the Board is of the opinion that any complaint may be resolved by mediation, it\nmay direct the parties concerned to attempt resolution of the dispute through such mediation\nby such mediator as the parties may mutually agree upon, or as provided for under any law\nfor the time being in force in India.",
      "bodyText": "If the Board is of the opinion that any complaint may be resolved by mediation, it\nmay direct the parties concerned to attempt resolution of the dispute through such mediation\nby such mediator as the parties may mutually agree upon, or as provided for under any law\nfor the time being in force in India.",
      "leadInText": "If the Board is of the opinion that any complaint may be resolved by mediation, it may direct the parties concerned to attempt resolution of the dispute through such mediation by such mediator as the parties may mutually agree upon, or as provided for under any law for the time being in force in India.",
      "textStatus": "PDF-extracted; Gazette PDF remains authoritative",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:31:unstructured:1",
      "@type": "dpdp:TextBlock",
      "parent": "act:section:31",
      "sourceText": "If the Board is of the opinion that any complaint may be resolved by mediation, it",
      "order": 0,
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023"
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:31:unstructured:2",
      "@type": "dpdp:TextBlock",
      "parent": "act:section:31",
      "sourceText": "may direct the parties concerned to attempt resolution of the dispute through such mediation",
      "order": 1,
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023"
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:31:unstructured:3",
      "@type": "dpdp:TextBlock",
      "parent": "act:section:31",
      "sourceText": "by such mediator as the parties may mutually agree upon, or as provided for under any law",
      "order": 2,
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023"
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:31:unstructured:4",
      "@type": "dpdp:TextBlock",
      "parent": "act:section:31",
      "sourceText": "for the time being in force in India.",
      "order": 3,
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023"
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:32",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:chapter:vii",
      "provisionLevel": "section",
      "sectionNumber": 32,
      "title": "Voluntary undertaking",
      "sourcePages": {
        "start": 16,
        "end": 16
      },
      "extractedSourceText": "32. (1) The Board may accept a voluntary undertaking in respect of any matter related\nto observance of the provisions of this Act from any person at any stage of a proceeding\nunder section 28.\n(2) The voluntary undertaking referred to in sub-section (1) may include an\nundertaking to take such action within such time as may be determined by the Board, or\nrefrain from taking such action, and or publicising such undertaking.\n(3) The Board may, after accepting the voluntary undertaking and with the consent of\nthe person who gave the voluntary undertaking vary the terms included in the voluntary\nundertaking.\n(4) The acceptance of the voluntary undertaking by the Board shall constitute a bar\non proceedings under the provisions of this Act as regards the contents of the voluntary\nundertaking, except in cases covered by sub-section (5).\n(5) Where a person fails to adhere to any term of the voluntary undertaking accepted\nby the Board, such breach shall be deemed to be breach of the provisions of this Act and\nthe Board may, after giving such person an opportunity of being heard, proceed in accordance\nwith the provisions of section",
      "bodyText": "(1) The Board may accept a voluntary undertaking in respect of any matter related\nto observance of the provisions of this Act from any person at any stage of a proceeding\nunder section 28.\n(2) The voluntary undertaking referred to in sub-section (1) may include an\nundertaking to take such action within such time as may be determined by the Board, or\nrefrain from taking such action, and or publicising such undertaking.\n(3) The Board may, after accepting the voluntary undertaking and with the consent of\nthe person who gave the voluntary undertaking vary the terms included in the voluntary\nundertaking.\n(4) The acceptance of the voluntary undertaking by the Board shall constitute a bar\non proceedings under the provisions of this Act as regards the contents of the voluntary\nundertaking, except in cases covered by sub-section (5).\n(5) Where a person fails to adhere to any term of the voluntary undertaking accepted\nby the Board, such breach shall be deemed to be breach of the provisions of this Act and\nthe Board may, after giving such person an opportunity of being heard, proceed in accordance\nwith the provisions of section",
      "leadInText": "",
