      "sourceText": "be credited to the Consolidated Fund of India.",
      "order": 1,
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023"
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:35",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:chapter:ix",
      "provisionLevel": "section",
      "sectionNumber": 35,
      "title": "Protection of action taken in good faith",
      "sourcePages": {
        "start": 17,
        "end": 17
      },
      "extractedSourceText": "35. No suit, prosecution or other legal proceedings shall lie against the Central\nGovernment, the Board, its Chairperson and any Member, officer or employee thereof for\nanything which is done or intended to be done in good faith under the provisions of this\nAct or the rules made thereunder.",
      "bodyText": "No suit, prosecution or other legal proceedings shall lie against the Central\nGovernment, the Board, its Chairperson and any Member, officer or employee thereof for\nanything which is done or intended to be done in good faith under the provisions of this\nAct or the rules made thereunder.",
      "leadInText": "No suit, prosecution or other legal proceedings shall lie against the Central Government, the Board, its Chairperson and any Member, officer or employee thereof for anything which is done or intended to be done in good faith under the provisions of this Act or the rules made thereunder.",
      "textStatus": "PDF-extracted; Gazette PDF remains authoritative",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:35:unstructured:1",
      "@type": "dpdp:TextBlock",
      "parent": "act:section:35",
      "sourceText": "No suit, prosecution or other legal proceedings shall lie against the Central",
      "order": 0,
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023"
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:35:unstructured:2",
      "@type": "dpdp:TextBlock",
      "parent": "act:section:35",
      "sourceText": "Government, the Board, its Chairperson and any Member, officer or employee thereof for",
      "order": 1,
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023"
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:35:unstructured:3",
      "@type": "dpdp:TextBlock",
      "parent": "act:section:35",
      "sourceText": "anything which is done or intended to be done in good faith under the provisions of this",
      "order": 2,
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023"
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:35:unstructured:4",
      "@type": "dpdp:TextBlock",
      "parent": "act:section:35",
      "sourceText": "Act or the rules made thereunder.",
      "order": 3,
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023"
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:36",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:chapter:ix",
      "provisionLevel": "section",
      "sectionNumber": 36,
      "title": "Power to call for information",
      "sourcePages": {
        "start": 17,
        "end": 17
      },
      "extractedSourceText": "36. The Central Government may, for the purposes of this Act, require the Board and\nany Data Fiduciary or intermediary to furnish such information as it may call for.",
      "bodyText": "The Central Government may, for the purposes of this Act, require the Board and\nany Data Fiduciary or intermediary to furnish such information as it may call for.",
      "leadInText": "The Central Government may, for the purposes of this Act, require the Board and any Data Fiduciary or intermediary to furnish such information as it may call for.",
      "textStatus": "PDF-extracted; Gazette PDF remains authoritative",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:36:unstructured:1",
      "@type": "dpdp:TextBlock",
      "parent": "act:section:36",
      "sourceText": "The Central Government may, for the purposes of this Act, require the Board and",
      "order": 0,
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023"
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:36:unstructured:2",
      "@type": "dpdp:TextBlock",
      "parent": "act:section:36",
      "sourceText": "any Data Fiduciary or intermediary to furnish such information as it may call for.",
      "order": 1,
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023"
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:37",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:chapter:ix",
      "provisionLevel": "section",
      "sectionNumber": 37,
      "title": "Power of Central Government to issue directions",
      "sourcePages": {
        "start": 17,
        "end": null
      },
      "extractedSourceText": "37. (1) The Central Government or any of its officers specially authorised by it in this\nbehalf may, upon receipt of a reference in writing from the Board that—\n(a) intimates the imposition of monetary penalty by the Board on a Data Fiduciary\nin two or more instances; and\n(b) advises, in the interests of the general public, the blocking for access by the\npublic to any information generated, transmitted, received, stored or hosted, in any\ncomputer resource that enables such Data Fiduciary to carry on any activity relating\nto offering of goods or services to Data Principals within the territory of India,\nafter giving an opportunity of being heard to that Data Fiduciary, on being satisfied that it\nis necessary or expedient so to do, in the interests of the general public, for reasons to be\nrecorded in writing, by order, direct any agency of the Central Government or any intermediary\nto block for access by the public or cause to be blocked for access by the public any such\ninformation.\n(2) Every intermediary who receives a direction issued under sub-section (1) shall be\nbound to comply with the same.\n(3) For the purposes of this section, the expressions “computer resource”,\n“information” and “intermediary” shall have the meanings respectively assigned to them in\nthe Information Technology Act, 2000.",
      "bodyText": "(1) The Central Government or any of its officers specially authorised by it in this\nbehalf may, upon receipt of a reference in writing from the Board that—\n(a) intimates the imposition of monetary penalty by the Board on a Data Fiduciary\nin two or more instances; and\n(b) advises, in the interests of the general public, the blocking for access by the\npublic to any information generated, transmitted, received, stored or hosted, in any\ncomputer resource that enables such Data Fiduciary to carry on any activity relating\nto offering of goods or services to Data Principals within the territory of India,\nafter giving an opportunity of being heard to that Data Fiduciary, on being satisfied that it\nis necessary or expedient so to do, in the interests of the general public, for reasons to be\nrecorded in writing, by order, direct any agency of the Central Government or any intermediary\nto block for access by the public or cause to be blocked for access by the public any such\ninformation.\n(2) Every intermediary who receives a direction issued under sub-section (1) shall be\nbound to comply with the same.\n(3) For the purposes of this section, the expressions “computer resource”,\n“information” and “intermediary” shall have the meanings respectively assigned to them in\nthe Information Technology Act, 2000.",
      "leadInText": "",
      "textStatus": "PDF-extracted; Gazette PDF remains authoritative",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
