      "depth": 1,
      "order": 0,
      "sourceText": "A Data Fiduciary,\nwho is of such class and is processing personal data for such corresponding purposes as are specified in\nThird Schedule, shall erase such personal data, unless its retention is necessary for compliance with any law\nfor the time being in force, or, for the corresponding time period specified in the Third Schedule, if the Data\nPrincipal neither approaches such Data Fiduciary for the performance of the specified purpose nor exercises\nher rights in relation to such processing.",
      "crossReferences": [
        {
          "referenceKind": "schedule",
          "sourcePhrase": "Third Schedule",
          "targetDocument": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
          "target": "rules:schedule:third",
          "resolutionStatus": "internal-resolved"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "rule:8:subrule:2",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
      "parent": "rule:8",
      "rootProvision": "rule:8",
      "provisionLevel": "subrule",
      "marker": "(2)",
      "markerToken": "2",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 1,
      "sourceText": "At least forty -eight hours before completion of the time period for erasure of personal data under this\nrule, the Data Fiduciary shall inform the Data Principal that such personal data shall be erased upon\ncompletion of such period, unless she logs into her user account or otherwise initiates contact with the Data\nFiduciary for the performance of the specified purpose or exercises her rights in relation to the processing\nof such personal data.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "rule:8:subrule:3",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
      "parent": "rule:8",
      "rootProvision": "rule:8",
      "provisionLevel": "subrule",
      "marker": "(3)",
      "markerToken": "3",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 2,
      "sourceText": "Without prejudice to sub-rules (1) and (2), a Data Fiduciary shall retain, in respect of any processing of\npersonal data undertaken by it or on its behalf by a Data Processor, such personal data, associated traffic\ndata and other logs of the processing for a minimum period of one year from the date of such processing,\nfor the purposes as specified in the Seventh Schedule, after which the Data Fiduciary shall cause such\npersonal data and logs to be erased, unless further retention is required for compliance with any other law\nfor the time being in force or notified by the Government.",
      "crossReferences": [
        {
          "referenceKind": "schedule",
          "sourcePhrase": "Seventh Schedule",
          "targetDocument": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
          "target": "rules:schedule:seventh",
          "resolutionStatus": "internal-resolved"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "rule:8:illustration:1",
      "@type": "dpdp:Illustration",
      "parent": "rule:8",
      "sourceText": "Case 1: X, a Data Principal purchases an e-book on an e -book platform Y. Once delivery is\ncompleted, the specified purpose of processing is served. The platform Y must retain the order details,\npersonal data, and logs of the processing (such as order confirmation, payment, and delivery events) for at\nleast one year from the date of the transaction, even if X deletes her account.\nCase 2: X, a company engages a cloud service provider C as its Data Processor to host customer\nrecords. X as the Data Fiduciary, is required to ensure that the C also retains the data and associated logs\nfor at least one year before erasure, unless any other applicable law requires a longer period.",
      "order": 3,
      "document": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025"
    },
    {
      "@id": "rule:9",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
      "provisionLevel": "rule",
      "ruleNumber": 9,
      "title": "Contact information of person to answer questions about processing",
      "sourcePages": {
        "start": 4,
        "end": 4
      },
      "extractedSourceText": "9. Contact information of person to answer questions about processing. — Every Data Fiduciary shall\nprominently publish on its website or app, and mention in every response to a communication for the\nexercise of the rights of a Data Principal under the Act, the business contact information of the Data\nProtection Officer, if applicable, or a person who is able to answer on behalf of the Data Fiduciary the\nquestions of the Data Principal about the processing of her personal data.",
      "bodyText": "Every Data Fiduciary shall\nprominently publish on its website or app, and mention in every response to a communication for the\nexercise of the rights of a Data Principal under the Act, the business contact information of the Data\nProtection Officer, if applicable, or a person who is able to answer on behalf of the Data Fiduciary the\nquestions of the Data Principal about the processing of her personal data.",
      "leadInText": "Every Data Fiduciary shall prominently publish on its website or app, and mention in every response to a communication for the exercise of the rights of a Data Principal under the Act, the business contact information of the Data Protection Officer, if applicable, or a person who is able to answer on behalf of the Data Fiduciary the questions of the Data Principal about the processing of her personal data.",
      "commencement": {
        "basis": "Rule 1",
        "effectiveDateDerived": "2027-05-13"
      },
      "implementsOrOperationalises": [
        "act:section:8"
      ],
      "delegationBasis": [
        "act:section:40:subsection:2:clause:h"
      ],
      "crossReferences": [],
      "textStatus": "PDF-extracted; Gazette PDF remains authoritative"
    },
