          "targetDocument": "ext:rights-persons-disabilities-act-2016",
          "resolutionStatus": "external-resolved-document",
          "context": "(2) In this rule, the expression— (a) “designated authority” shall mean an authority designated under section 15 of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act, 2016 (49 of 2016) to support persons with disabilities in exercise of their legal capacity;"
        },
        {
          "referenceKind": "section",
          "sourcePhrase": "section 13",
          "targetDocument": "ext:national-trust-act-1999",
          "resolutionStatus": "external-resolved-document",
          "context": "(c) “local level committee” shall mean a local level committee constituted under section 13 of the National Trust for the Welfare of Persons with Autism, Cerebral Palsy, Mental Retardation and Multiple Disabilities Act, 1999 (44 of 1999);"
        }
      ],
      "textStatus": "PDF-extracted; Gazette PDF remains authoritative"
    },
    {
      "@id": "rule:11:subrule:2",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
      "parent": "rule:11",
      "rootProvision": "rule:11",
      "provisionLevel": "subrule",
      "marker": "(2)",
      "markerToken": "2",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 5,
      "sourceText": "In this rule, the expression—",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "rule:11:subrule:2:clause:a",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
      "parent": "rule:11:subrule:2",
      "rootProvision": "rule:11",
      "provisionLevel": "clause",
      "marker": "(a)",
      "markerToken": "a",
      "depth": 2,
      "order": 6,
      "sourceText": "“designated authority” shall mean an authority designated under section 15 of the Rights of Persons\nwith Disabilities Act, 2016 (49 of 2016) to support persons with disabilities in exercise of their\nlegal capacity;",
      "crossReferences": [
        {
          "referenceKind": "section",
          "sourcePhrase": "section 15",
          "targetDocument": "ext:rights-persons-disabilities-act-2016",
          "resolutionStatus": "external-resolved-document",
          "context": "“designated authority” shall mean an authority designated under section 15 of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act, 2016 (49 of 2016) to support persons with disabilities in exercise of their legal capacity;"
        }
      ],
      "_has_children": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "rule:11:subrule:2:clause:b",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
      "parent": "rule:11:subrule:2",
      "rootProvision": "rule:11",
      "provisionLevel": "clause",
      "marker": "(b)",
      "markerToken": "b",
      "depth": 2,
      "order": 7,
      "sourceText": "“law applicable to guardianship” shall mean, —",
      "crossReferences": [],
      "_has_children": true
    },
    {
      "@id": "rule:11:subrule:2:clause:b:subclause:i",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
      "parent": "rule:11:subrule:2:clause:b",
      "rootProvision": "rule:11",
      "provisionLevel": "subclause",
      "marker": "(i)",
      "markerToken": "i",
      "depth": 3,
      "order": 8,
      "sourceText": "in relation to an individual who has long term physical, mental, intellectual or sensory\nimpairment which, in interaction with barriers, hinders her full and effective participation\nin society equally with others and who despite being provided adequate and appropriate\nsupport is unable to take legally binding decisions, the provisions of law contained in\nRights of Persons with Disabilities Act, 2016 (49 of 2016) and the rules made thereunder;\nand",
      "crossReferences": [],
      "_has_children": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "rule:11:subrule:2:clause:b:subclause:ii",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
      "parent": "rule:11:subrule:2:clause:b",
      "rootProvision": "rule:11",
      "provisionLevel": "subclause",
      "marker": "(ii)",
      "markerToken": "ii",
      "depth": 3,
      "order": 9,
      "sourceText": "in relation to a person who is suffering from any of the conditions relating to autism,\ncerebral palsy, mental retardation or a combination of such conditions and includes a\nperson suffering from severe multiple disability, the provisions of law of the National Trust\nfor the Welfare of Persons with Autism, Cerebral Palsy, Mental Retardation and Multiple\nDisabilities Act, 1999 (44 of 1999) and the rules made thereunder;",
      "crossReferences": [],
      "_has_children": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "rule:11:subrule:2:clause:c",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
      "parent": "rule:11:subrule:2",
      "rootProvision": "rule:11",
      "provisionLevel": "clause",
      "marker": "(c)",
      "markerToken": "c",
      "depth": 2,
      "order": 10,
      "sourceText": "“local level committee” shall mean a local level committee constituted under section 13 of the\nNational Trust for the Welfare of Persons with Autism, Cerebral Palsy, Mental Retardation and\nMultiple Disabilities Act, 1999 (44 of 1999);",
      "crossReferences": [
        {
          "referenceKind": "section",
          "sourcePhrase": "section 13",
          "targetDocument": "ext:national-trust-act-1999",
          "resolutionStatus": "external-resolved-document",
          "context": "“local level committee” shall mean a local level committee constituted under section 13 of the National Trust for the Welfare of Persons with Autism, Cerebral Palsy, Mental Retardation and Multiple Disabilities Act, 1999 (44 of 1999);"
        }
      ],
      "_has_children": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "rule:11:subrule:2:clause:d",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
      "parent": "rule:11:subrule:2",
      "rootProvision": "rule:11",
      "provisionLevel": "clause",
      "marker": "(d)",
      "markerToken": "d",
      "depth": 2,
      "order": 11,
      "sourceText": "“person with disability” shall mean and include—",
      "crossReferences": [],
      "_has_children": true
    },
    {
      "@id": "rule:11:subrule:2:clause:d:subclause:i",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
      "parent": "rule:11:subrule:2:clause:d",
      "rootProvision": "rule:11",
      "provisionLevel": "subclause",
      "marker": "(i)",
      "markerToken": "i",
      "depth": 3,
      "order": 12,
      "sourceText": "an individual who has long term physical, mental, intellectual or sensory impairment\nwhich, in interaction with barriers, hinders her full and effective participation in society\nequally with others and who, despite being provided adequate and appropriate support, is\nunable to take legally binding decisions; and",
      "crossReferences": [],
      "_has_children": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "rule:11:subrule:2:clause:d:subclause:ii",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
      "parent": "rule:11:subrule:2:clause:d",
      "rootProvision": "rule:11",
      "provisionLevel": "subclause",
      "marker": "(ii)",
      "markerToken": "ii",
      "depth": 3,
      "order": 13,
      "sourceText": "an individual who is suffering from any of the conditions relating to autism, cerebral palsy,\nmental retardation or a combination of any two or more of such conditions and includes an\nindividual suffering from severe multiple disability and who, despite being provided\nadequate and appropriate support, is unable to take legally binding decisions.",
      "crossReferences": [],
      "_has_children": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "rule:12",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
      "provisionLevel": "rule",
      "ruleNumber": 12,
      "title": "Exemptions from certain obligations applicable to processing of personal data of child",
      "sourcePages": {
        "start": 6,
        "end": 6
      },
      "extractedSourceText": "12. Exemptions from certain obligations applicable to processing of personal data of child . — (1) The\nprovisions of sub -sections (1) and (3) of section 9 of the Act shall not be applicable to processing of\npersonal data of a child by such class of Data Fiduciaries as are specified in Part A of Fourth Schedule,\nsubject to such conditions as are specified in the said Part.\n(2) The provisions of sub-sections (1) and (3) of section 9 of the Act shall not be applicable to processing of\npersonal data of a child for such purposes as are specified in Part B of Fourth Schedule , subject to such\nconditions as are specified in the said Part.",
      "bodyText": "(1) The\nprovisions of sub -sections (1) and (3) of section 9 of the Act shall not be applicable to processing of\npersonal data of a child by such class of Data Fiduciaries as are specified in Part A of Fourth Schedule,\nsubject to such conditions as are specified in the said Part.\n(2) The provisions of sub-sections (1) and (3) of section 9 of the Act shall not be applicable to processing of\npersonal data of a child for such purposes as are specified in Part B of Fourth Schedule , subject to such\nconditions as are specified in the said Part.",
      "leadInText": "",
      "commencement": {
