      "depth": 1,
      "order": 8,
      "sourceText": "The inquiry by the Board shall be completed within a period of six months from the date of receipt of\nthe intimation, complaint, reference or direction under section 27 of the Act, unless such period is extended\nby it, for reasons to be recorded in writing, for a further period not exceeding three months at a time.",
      "crossReferences": [
        {
          "referenceKind": "section",
          "sourcePhrase": "section 27",
          "targetDocument": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
          "target": "act:section:27",
          "resolutionStatus": "internal-resolved-root",
          "context": "The inquiry by the Board shall be completed within a period of six months from the date of receipt of the intimation, complaint, reference or direction under section 27 of the Act, unless such period is extended by it, for reasons to be recorded in writing, for a further period not exceeding three months at a time."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "rule:20",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
      "provisionLevel": "rule",
      "ruleNumber": 20,
      "title": "Functioning of Board as digital office",
      "sourcePages": {
        "start": 8,
        "end": 8
      },
      "extractedSourceText": "20. Functioning of Board as digital office . — The Board shall function as a digital office, without\nprejudice to its power to summon and enforce the attendance of any person and examine her on oath, may\nadopt techno-legal measures to conduct proceedings in a manner that does not require physical presence of\nany individual.",
      "bodyText": "The Board shall function as a digital office, without\nprejudice to its power to summon and enforce the attendance of any person and examine her on oath, may\nadopt techno-legal measures to conduct proceedings in a manner that does not require physical presence of\nany individual.",
      "leadInText": "The Board shall function as a digital office, without prejudice to its power to summon and enforce the attendance of any person and examine her on oath, may adopt techno-legal measures to conduct proceedings in a manner that does not require physical presence of any individual.",
