    {
      "@id": "rule:23",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
      "provisionLevel": "rule",
      "ruleNumber": 23,
      "title": "Calling for information from Data Fiduciary or intermediary",
      "sourcePages": {
        "start": 9,
        "end": 9
      },
      "extractedSourceText": "23. Calling for information from Data Fiduciary or intermediary. — (1) The Central Government may,\nfor such purposes of the Act as are specified in Seventh Schedule, acting through the corresponding\nauthorised person specified in the said Schedule, require any Data Fiduciary or intermediary to furnish such\ninformation as may be called for, within the specified period as may be given in such.\n(2) Where the disclosure of furnishing of information as referred to in sub -rule (1) is likely to prejudicially\naffect the sovereignty and integrity of India or security of the State, the Central Government may require\nthe Data Fiduciary or intermediary to not disclose such furnishing to affected Data Principal or any other\nperson except with the previous permission, in writing, of the authorised person.\n(3) For the purposes of this rule, the expression “intermediary” shall have the same meaning as assigned to\nit in the Information Technology Act, 2000 (21 of 2000).",
      "bodyText": "(1) The Central Government may,\nfor such purposes of the Act as are specified in Seventh Schedule, acting through the corresponding\nauthorised person specified in the said Schedule, require any Data Fiduciary or intermediary to furnish such\ninformation as may be called for, within the specified period as may be given in such.\n(2) Where the disclosure of furnishing of information as referred to in sub -rule (1) is likely to prejudicially\naffect the sovereignty and integrity of India or security of the State, the Central Government may require\nthe Data Fiduciary or intermediary to not disclose such furnishing to affected Data Principal or any other\nperson except with the previous permission, in writing, of the authorised person.\n(3) For the purposes of this rule, the expression “intermediary” shall have the same meaning as assigned to\nit in the Information Technology Act, 2000 (21 of 2000).",
      "leadInText": "",
      "commencement": {
        "basis": "Rule 1",
        "effectiveDateDerived": "2027-05-13"
      },
