    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:33:subsection:1",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:33",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:33",
      "provisionLevel": "subsection",
      "marker": "(1)",
      "markerToken": "1",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 0,
      "sourceText": "If the Board determines on conclusion of an inquiry that breach of the provisions of this Act or the rules made thereunder by a person is significant, it may, after giving the person an opportunity of being heard, impose such monetary penalty specified in the Schedule.",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "rule:5:subrule:1",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
      "parent": "rule:5",
      "rootProvision": "rule:5",
      "provisionLevel": "subrule",
      "marker": "(1)",
      "markerToken": "1",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 0,
      "sourceText": "Processing the personal data of a Data Principal under this rule shall be done following the standards specified in Second Schedule.",
      "crossReferences": [
        {
          "referenceKind": "schedule",
          "sourcePhrase": "Second Schedule",
          "targetDocument": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
          "target": "rules:schedule:second",
          "resolutionStatus": "internal-resolved"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "rule:11:subrule:1",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
      "parent": "rule:11",
      "rootProvision": "rule:11",
      "provisionLevel": "subrule",
      "marker": "(1)",
      "markerToken": "1",
      "depth": 1,
      "order": 0,
      "sourceText": "A Data Fiduciary, while obtaining verifiable consent from an individual identifying herself as the lawful guardian of a person with disability, shall observe due diligence to verify that such guardian is appointed by a court of law, or by a designated authority or by a local level committee, under the law applicable to guardianship.",
      "crossReferences": [
        {
          "referenceKind": "section",
          "sourcePhrase": "section 15",
          "targetDocument": "ext:rights-persons-disabilities-act-2016",
          "resolutionStatus": "external-resolved-document",
          "context": "(2) In this rule, the expression— (a) “designated authority” shall mean an authority designated under section 15 of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act, 2016 (49 of 2016) to support persons with disabilities in exercise of their legal capacity;"
        },
        {
          "referenceKind": "section",
          "sourcePhrase": "section 13",
          "targetDocument": "ext:national-trust-act-1999",
          "resolutionStatus": "external-resolved-document",
          "context": "(c) “local level committee” shall mean a local level committee constituted under section 13 of the National Trust for the Welfare of Persons with Autism, Cerebral Palsy, Mental Retardation and Multiple Disabilities Act, 1999 (44 of 1999);"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "act:section:44:subsection:1:clause:i",
      "@type": "dpdp:LegalProvision",
      "document": "doc:dpdp-act-2023",
      "parent": "act:section:44:subsection:1",
      "rootProvision": "act:section:44",
      "provisionLevel": "clause",
      "marker": "(i)",
      "markerToken": "i",
      "depth": 2,
      "order": 0,
      "sourceText": "the Appellate Tribunal under the Information Technology Act, 2000",
      "crossReferences": []
    },
