        "dpdp:NormativeStatement"
      ],
      "sourceDocument": "doc:dpdp-rules-2025",
      "sourceProvision": "rule:8:subrule:1",
      "sourceText": "A Data Fiduciary, who is of such class and is processing personal data for such corresponding purposes as are specified in Third Schedule, shall erase such personal data, unless its retention is necessary for compliance with any law for the time being in force, or, for the corresponding time period specified in the Third Schedule, if the Data Principal neither approaches such Data Fiduciary for the performance of the specified purpose nor exercises her rights in relation to such processing.",
      "propositionText": "A Data Fiduciary, who is of such class and is processing personal data for such corresponding purposes as are specified in Third Schedule, shall erase such personal data, unless its retention is necessary for compliance with any law for the time being in force, or, for the corresponding time period specified in the Third Schedule, if the Data Principal neither approaches such Data Fiduciary for the performance of the specified purpose nor exercises her rights in relation to such processing.",
